    "result_text": "The build passes and the test is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of owners whose email domain is on a disposable-domain blocklist, in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the controller handling `POST /api/owners`):\n\n1. **Added a blocklist constant** \u2014 `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` containing `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, and `guerrillamail.com`.\n\n2. **Extended `normalizeEmail(...)`** \u2014 after the existing syntactic validation and lowercasing, it extracts the domain (part after `@`) and throws `InvalidOwnerFieldsException(List.of(\"email\"))` if it's on the blocklist. That exception maps to a **400 Bad Request** with `email` in the `errors` array, consistent with the existing invalid-email handling.\n\n3. Added the `java.util.Set` import.\n\nThe check reuses the existing normalization path, so it applies to both create and update flows and matches domains case-insensitively (comparison happens against the already-lowercased value). The new acceptance test `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0).",
